%h2 Goal

%p
  The proposed Networking for AI Research Group (NET4AI) brings together
  researchers and the Internet community to investigate the networking
  foundations of distributed AI systems spanning multiple stakeholders.
  It provides a forum for long-term architectural research beyond the
  immediate requirements addressed by IETF working groups.

%h2 Scope

%p
  NET4AI explores Internet support for autonomous agents, decentralized
  AI systems, and communication architectures for AI ecosystems. Its scope
  extends beyond individual datacenters to the challenges of operating AI
  workloads across networks and administrative domains.

%h2 Background

%p
  Generative and agentic AI have prompted new protocol discussions in the
  IETF and growing research interest in networking for training, inference,
  and large language model serving. NET4AI complements these activities by
  examining longer-term questions about Internet architecture, decentralization,
  and support for networked AI systems.

%h2 Research areas

%ul
  %li Adapting Internet protocols to support AI workloads.
  %li Testbeds and benchmarks for research on agentic network management.
  %li Communication protocols tailored to agents beyond human-readable, real-time interactions.
  %li Caching and content distribution for AI, including key-value cache distribution for inference beyond a single datacenter.
  %li Agent identity, naming, and addressing across domains, including decentralized approaches to trustworthy agent communication.
  %li Security requirements introduced by agentic AI.

%h2 Mode of Operation

%p
  NET4AI will assess and develop experimental tools, including simulators
  and testbeds, and collect and share datasets for reproducible experiments.
  The group will encourage research on networked AI systems, new architectures
  such as key-value-cache-centric and mixture-of-experts systems, inter-datacenter
  communication, and security. It will also explore principled approaches to
  communication among agents.

%p
  The proposed charter and current group information are available on the
  %a{ :href => "https://datatracker.ietf.org/rg/net4ai/about/" } IETF Datatracker.

%h2 Membership

%p
  Membership in the #{acronym} is open to all interested parties.
